From 5b0e574e46bd17bf0e13ce0f9836456f921c6639 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <dev@infoverify.local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 17:12:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use real slip photos on NIN_Phone page, fix WhatsApp float,
 mark Information Slip Coming Soon
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- TierCardGrid (shared.tsx) gains optional imageFor and disabledFor props:
  imageFor swaps the abstract SlipIcon SVGs for a real photo from
  public/branding; disabledFor dims a tile, blocks selection, and shows
  a 'Coming Soon' badge instead of an endless 'Price loading…'.
- NinPhoneVerificationPage: both the NIN and Phone tier grids now use
  the real branding photos. Information Slip is marked disabledFor
  (Techhub's API has no information-slip endpoint - only
  premium/standard/regular/vnin - so it stays unselectable, but now
  reads 'Coming Soon' instead of looking like a stuck price load).
- WhatsappFloat: replaced the generic lucide MessageCircle with an
  actual WhatsApp glyph, and added a sidebarOffset prop (lg:left-72)
  so it clears the app shell's fixed 256px sidebar instead of sitting
  on top of the Logout link. AppShell now passes sidebarOffset; the
  public LandingPage keeps the plain left-4 position.
---
 web/src/components/AppShell.tsx               |  2 +-
 web/src/components/WhatsappFloat.tsx          | 16 ++++--
 web/src/components/verification/shared.tsx    | 56 +++++++++++++------
 .../verification/NinPhoneVerificationPage.tsx | 27 ++++++++-
 4 files changed, 76 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

